# Code activity shown in the hero (lib/activity.ts). Only daily counts are published.
# Your gitlab.com username. Enable "Include private contributions on my profile"
# in GitLab > Preferences > User settings > Profile so private work is counted.
GITLAB_USERNAME=
# Recommended: read-only GitLab token (scope read_api). Contributions are then counted from the
# authenticated events API (dates and action names only) instead of the public calendar, which
# gitlab.com rate-limits per IP (HTTP 429). Also gives the exact time of the latest push.
# GITLAB_TOKEN=
# Optional: another GitLab instance (defaults to https://gitlab.com)
# GITLAB_URL=https://gitlab.com
# Optional: GitHub account (defaults to claudemoz) and a read-only token to raise the API rate limit
# GITHUB_USERNAME=
# GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Calendly booking page shown in the "Prendre rendez-vous" dialog (button hidden when empty)
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CALENDLY_URL=https://calendly.com/ton-nom/30min

# Cal.com booking page (alternative to Calendly), e.g. https://cal.com/ton-nom/30min
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CALCOM_URL=
# Which service the "Prendre rendez-vous" button opens: calendly (default) or calcom.
# To compare without rebuilding, add ?rdv=calcom or ?rdv=calendly to the page URL.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BOOKING_PROVIDER=calendly
